WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.725
macOS forensics is the preservation and analysis of evidence from Apple desktop and laptop systems.

00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:21.537
The system may be an employee MacBook, an iMac, a developer workstation, an enterprise-managed device, a virtualized testing system, or an Apple Silicon platform with modern security controls.

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:33.008
The forensic goal is to understand what happened, when it happened, what users or systems were involved, and what evidence supports the conclusion.

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:41.670
macOS investigations often support DFIR, insider investigations, endpoint response, user activity reconstruction, policy investigations, and malware triage.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:57.355
Evidence may exist in user home directories, system and user libraries, unified logs, application data, preferences, launch items, file metadata, quarantine attributes, browser artifacts, endpoint security telemetry, and cloud or identity records.

00:00:57.355 --> 00:01:01.335
No single source tells the entire story.

00:01:01.335 --> 00:01:13.274
Authorization and careful handling matter because Macs often contain sensitive business records, source code, credentials, personal files, messaging data, browser history, and regulated information.

00:01:13.274 --> 00:01:23.340
Analysts should work under approved authority, collect only what is needed, preserve it appropriately, and document how evidence was handled.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:31.065
Enterprise management tools may help collection, but they also add their own artifacts and constraints.

00:01:31.065 --> 00:01:34.109
Evidence integrity is the foundation.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:40.898
Investigator activity can alter timestamps, create logs, update caches, or change volatile state.

00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:50.964
Sometimes live response is necessary, especially when a device is remote or encrypted, but actions should be deliberate and recorded.

00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:55.412
Strong macOS forensics is careful, contextual, and evidence-driven.

00:01:55.412 --> 00:02:01.264
It avoids overclaiming from isolated artifacts and focuses on defensible conclusions.
